{"tool_name":"porechop_abi","contents":["bioconda","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"porechop_abi","version":"0.5.1","home":"https://github.com/bonsai-team/Porechop_ABI","documentation":"https://github.com/bonsai-team/Porechop_ABI/blob/master/README.md","license":"GPL-3.0-or-later","summary":"Adapter inferrence and removal of Oxford Nanopore reads.","identifiers":["biotools:porechop_abi"],"license_file":"LICENSE","build":{"entry_points":["porechop_abi = porechop_abi.porechop_abi:main"],"number":0,"run_exports":[null],"script":["export LDFLAGS=\"${LDFLAGS} -L${PREFIX}/lib\"","export CPPFLAGS=\"${CPPFLAGS} -I${PREFIX}/include\"","export CXXFLAGS=\"${CXXFLAGS} -std=c++17 -pedantic\"","export CXXFLAGS=\"${CXXFLAGS} -march=x86-64-v3\"","export CXXFLAGS=\"${CXXFLAGS} -march=armv8-a\"","export CXXFLAGS=\"${CXXFLAGS} -march=armv8.4-a\"","export CXXFLAGS=\"${CXXFLAGS} -Dbinary_function=__binary_function -Dunary_function=__unary_function\"","-m pip install . --no-deps --no-build-isolation --no-cache-dir --use-pep517 -vvv"],"skip":true},"requirements":{"build":[null,"make","pkg-config"],"host":["python","setuptools","pip","networkx","libgomp","llvm-openmp","zlib"],"run":["python","networkx","libgomp","llvm-openmp"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/bonsai-team/Porechop_ABI/archive/0bc9f17f31d4ec1dcbab4796871cc09324cc143b.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["porechop_abi -h"]}},"biotools":{"id":"porechop_abi","home":"https://github.com/bonsai-team/Porechop_ABI","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Porechop_ABI (ab initio) is an extension of Porechop whose purpose is to process adapter sequences in ONT reads.","addition_date":"2022-12-07T14:31:52.494999Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:57:04.669626Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"version":["0.5.0"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:porechop_abi","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Quentin Bonenfant"},{"name":"H\u00e9l\u00e8ne Touzet","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-5305-9987"},{"name":"Laurent No\u00e9","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-1170-8376"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Base-calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3185"},{"term":"Demultiplexing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3933"},{"term":"Primer removal","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3237"},{"term":"Sequence trimming","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3192"},{"term":"k-mer counting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3472"}]}],"name":"Porechop_ABI","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"pauffret","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioadv/vbac085","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: Oxford Nanopore Technologies (ONT) sequencing has become very popular over the past few years and offers a cost-effective solution for many genomic and transcriptomic projects. One distinctive feature of the technology is that the protocol includes the ligation of adapters to both ends of each fragment. Those adapters should then be removed before downstream analyses, either during the basecalling step or by explicit trimming. This basic task may be tricky when the definition of the adapter sequence is not well documented. Results: We have developed a new method to scan a set of ONT reads to see if it contains adapters, without any prior knowledge on the sequence of the potential adapters, and then trim out those adapters. The algorithm is based on approximate k-mers and is able to discover adapter sequences based on their frequency alone. The method was successfully tested on a variety of ONT datasets with different flowcells, sequencing kits and basecallers.","authors":[{"name":"Bonenfant Q."},{"name":"Noe L."},{"name":"Touzet H."}],"citationCount":23,"date":"2023-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics Advances","title":"Porechop ABI: Discovering unknown adapters in Oxford Nanopore Technology sequencing reads for downstream trimming"},"pmcid":"PMC9869717","pmid":"36698762"}],"topic":[{"ter